.TH MANANNAN 8 "" "Manannan @PROJECT_VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
manannan \- plugin-based dynamic DNS updater
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B manannan
.I config.yaml
.br
.B manannan \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B manannan
reads a value from a source plugin, typically the host's public IP address,
and reconciles it with every record held by one or more registry plugins,
typically DNS providers. It repeats on the cadence the configuration sets
until it receives SIGINT or SIGTERM. Each record is checked and updated
independently, so a failure in one zone or account does not hold up the
others; a failed record is retried on the next cycle.
.PP
It normally runs as
.BR manannan.service ,
which reads the configuration from
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_SYSCONFDIR@/manannan/manannan.yaml
and the environment from
.IR @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_SYSCONFDIR@/manannan/environment .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The
.B manannan
block sets
.B cadence
(an integer and one of ms, s, m or h),
.B log_level
(debug, info, warn or error),
.B source
(one source plugin),
.B registries
(a list of registry plugins) and
.B plugin_directories
(directories scanned for plugins). Each plugin reads its own block at
.BI source. name
or
.BI registry. name\fR.
A value written as
.BI ${ NAME }
is read from the environment variable
.IR NAME .
.PP
The bundled plugins are
.B amazon_check_ip
and
.BR aws_route53 .
Their settings are described in the README at
https://github.com/tomdionysus/mannanan.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
Overrides
.B log_level
when set and not empty.
.TP
.BR AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID ", " AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY ", " AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
The credentials
.B aws_route53
uses for any record without credentials of its own.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_SYSCONFDIR@/manannan/manannan.yaml
The configuration, readable by the service's unprivileged user. It holds no
secrets.
.TP
.I @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_SYSCONFDIR@/manannan/environment
Keys for the service, readable by root only.
.TP
.I @MANANNAN_PLUGIN_DIR@
The bundled plugins.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after a clean shutdown, 1 when the configuration or a plugin is refused,
2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
